    "finishStory": {
      "origin": "suggested",
      "teacherReviewRequired": true,
      "markedParagraph": "The [Philistines] defeated Israel and captured the Ark of the [Covenant]. The Israelites had hoped the ark would [save] them, but the Ark was not some magic good luck box. The Philistines placed the ark in the temple of their idol [Dagon]. His statue [fell] down two times and broke into pieces. In the city of [Ashdod], people suffered painful [growths]. The Philistines kept sending the ark away to other [cities]. They finally put it on a [cart] pulled by two [cows]. Guided by God, the cows went [straight] back toward [Israel], mooing the entire way."
    },
